# Ansible Architecture Rules

## Role Structure
Every role uses the full directory structure. Initialize with `ansible-galaxy role init`:
```
roles/{rolename}/
  tasks/        — main.yml + install.yml + configure.yml
  handlers/     — main.yml (service restart handlers only)
  defaults/     — main.yml (user-overridable defaults)
  vars/         — main.yml (internal non-overridable values)
  files/        — static files copied as-is
  templates/    — Jinja2 templates (.j2)
  meta/         — main.yml (galaxy_info, dependencies)
  molecule/     — default/ test scenario
```

## One Responsibility Per Role
A role that installs AND configures AND deploys is three roles. Examples:
- `nginx_install` — installs the nginx package
- `nginx_configure` — writes vhost configs from templates
- `nginx_tls` — manages TLS certificates

Compose multiple roles in a playbook. Never put everything in one role.

## defaults vs vars
- `defaults/main.yml` — values users **should** override (port numbers, worker counts, log paths). Lowest precedence.
- `vars/main.yml` — internal values that **should not** be overridden (package names, internal paths). Higher precedence.
- Never define configurable values inline in tasks — always reference a variable from defaults.

## Handlers for Restarts
Use `notify: restart nginx` in tasks. Define handler in `handlers/main.yml`:
```yaml
- name: restart nginx
  ansible.builtin.service:
    name: nginx
    state: restarted
```
Never use `ansible.builtin.service` with `state: restarted` directly in a task — it runs unconditionally on every play, destroying idempotency.

## Become Discipline
- Use `become: true` only on individual tasks that require root
- Do not set `become: true` at the play level unless every single task needs root
- Always document why become is needed in a task comment when non-obvious

## Tags
Tag tasks by phase and component to allow targeted runs:
```yaml
- name: Install nginx package
  ansible.builtin.package:
    name: "{{ nginx_package_name }}"
  tags: [install, nginx]

- name: Write nginx configuration
  ansible.builtin.template:
    src: nginx.conf.j2
    dest: /etc/nginx/nginx.conf
  tags: [configure, nginx]
```

## No shell/command for Idempotent Work
Use specific modules: `package`, `file`, `template`, `service`, `copy`, `user`, `group`.
Use `ansible.builtin.shell` or `ansible.builtin.command` only when no module exists.
When you must use shell/command, add proper idempotency:
```yaml
- name: Run custom script only when needed
  ansible.builtin.command: /usr/local/bin/setup.sh
  changed_when: setup_result.rc == 0
  register: setup_result
  when: not setup_already_done.stat.exists
```
